  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Safe Programming Syria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conduct Safe Programming (SP) self -assessment and consultation workshop with field staff to identify specific gaps in understanding and committing to SP standards &#x2013; with 15 key staff from the three hubs and country office.  Conduct Action Planning workshop with key staff to develop specific, timely, organizational, programmatic, and departmental actions needed to improve quality application and enforcement of SP measures. &#x2013; with Area Managers (AMs), Team Leaders  (TLs), heads of support functions and Advisors.  Development of contextualized SP, comprehensive checklists per programme/department with responsibility/accountability roles defined clearly. The measures in the checklist should be informed by the SP self -assessment findings and action plan.  Development of brief, SP checklist tailored for the daily use of field staff and Protection Officer to guide and enable their observation and reporting.  Roll -out training/coaching sessions to field staff, field support personnel (FSPs) and managers to introduce them to the checklists and train them to use adequately &#x2013; targeting all staff and FSPs in around 10 sessions. Design a system for the field staff to report internally on SP observations; gaps and trends, and for managers to address timely and correct accordingly.  Maintain regular analysis of SP M&amp;E (Monitoring &amp; Evaluation) data at project and programme levels and timely sharing and tackling of findings/red flags, during project cycle management and programme quality meetings.  Ensure available, financial capacity to enable corrective measures.</narrative>
  </description>
